<item>
  <title><![CDATA[Linen in the Off-Season]]></title>
  <link>http://localhost:8885/2026/10/15/linen-in-the-off-season/</link>
  <pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
  <dc:creator>marketing</dc:creator>
  <guid isPermaLink="false">http://localhost:8885/2026/10/15/linen-in-the-off-season/</guid>
  <description/>
  <content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Linen is supposed to be a summer fabric. We disagree. Layered under a coarse knit or a canvas chore coat, a washed linen shirt carries its rumpled ease straight through to November.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The trick is to embrace the creases. Linen that has been ironed flat looks nervous. Linen that has been lived in looks like it knows something.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Look for heavier weights — 200 grams and up — in chalk, flax, and the faintest grey.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
