<item>
  <title><![CDATA[The Folded Stack]]></title>
  <link>http://localhost:8885/2026/09/24/the-folded-stack/</link>
  <pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:45:00 +0000</pubDate>
  <dc:creator>marketing</dc:creator>
  <guid isPermaLink="false">http://localhost:8885/2026/09/24/the-folded-stack/</guid>
  <description/>
  <content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There is a particular pleasure in a pile of clean, folded clothes. It is an image of order and of care, of time spent on something no one else will see.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Folding is a small ritual of maintenance. It is how garments last. Shoulders that hang too long stretch; knits that are folded keep their shape for decades.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Consider this an argument for owning fewer things and treating them better.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
