<item>
  <title><![CDATA[Inside the Small Boutique]]></title>
  <link>http://localhost:8885/2026/09/17/inside-the-small-boutique/</link>
  <pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
  <dc:creator>marketing</dc:creator>
  <guid isPermaLink="false">http://localhost:8885/2026/09/17/inside-the-small-boutique/</guid>
  <description/>
  <content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Big retail sells volume. Small boutiques sell a point of view. Step into one and you are stepping into someone's taste — a yellow tunic hung beside raw denim, a ceramic bowl on the counter that is not for sale.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These shops are fragile. They depend on regulars and word of mouth. They are also where fashion actually happens, far from the runway.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This month we visited five of them. The full list is coming in our next issue.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
