<item>
  <title><![CDATA[Monochrome Minimum]]></title>
  <link>http://localhost:8885/2026/09/10/monochrome-minimum/</link>
  <pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
  <dc:creator>marketing</dc:creator>
  <guid isPermaLink="false">http://localhost:8885/2026/09/10/monochrome-minimum/</guid>
  <description/>
  <content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Black, white, and one shade of grey. That is the entire rule for this experiment: thirty days, three colors, no exceptions.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What we found is that constraint does not flatten style — it sharpens it. Without color to lean on, texture and proportion have to do the work.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
